{"user": "Down 20-40, only 4 empty squares left (a1,h1,g2,a3), my legal moves are a1, g2, a3. Which move actually gives me the best final result, walk me through why?", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T22:34:50.110608+00:00", "assistant": "**a3** is best \u2014 it actually wins the endgame for Black.\n\nLine to see the idea:\n\n1. **Black a3** flips along toward **e7** and **c3**.  \n2. Now **White has no legal move**, so White must **pass**.  \n3. Then play **a1**. White still has no move.  \n4. Then play **h1**, flipping the whole top edge back.  \n5. Finally play **g2**.\n\nBest sequence: **a3, pass, a1, pass, h1, pass, g2**  \nFinal count: **Black 41 \u2013 White 23**.\n\nWhy not the corner first? **a1** is a corner, but here it gives White **a3**, which breaks your tempo. **a3** first is powerful because it forces passes and lets you take the remaining key squares yourself.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T22:34:50.110608+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T22:34:55.110608+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Solution Request": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Solution Request": 1.0}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"], "gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Move Verdict": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 3, "General Principle": 2, "Board Report": 1}, "confidence": {"Move Verdict": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 1.0, "General Principle": 0.6666666666666666, "Board Report": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Move Verdict",