{"user": "Looking back \u2014 why wasn't grabbing the a1 corner immediately the obvious best move? I thought corners were always the top priority in Othello.", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T22:35:05.110608+00:00", "assistant": "Corners are **usually** top priority because once you take them, they can\u2019t be flipped.\n\nBut here the key was: **could White take a1 if you didn\u2019t take it immediately?**  \nAfter **Black a3**, White had **no legal move**, so they had to pass. That means **a1 was still yours next turn anyway**.\n\nSo:\n\n- **a1 immediately** = safe corner, but it gives White a usable reply at **a3**, costing you tempo/discs.\n- **a3 first** = White must pass, then you still get **a1**, then keep taking the rest.\n\nIn endgames, the best move is often the one that **controls move order and forces passes**, not the one that grabs the biggest-looking square first. Here, **a3 didn\u2019t sacrifice the corner \u2014 it delayed taking it while preventing White from moving.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T22:35:05.110608+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T22:35:10.110608+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Common Ground Question": 1, "Think Aloud": 1, "Metacomment": 1}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333, "Think Aloud": 0.3333333333333333, "Metacomment": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle", "Hint"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle", "Hint"], "votes": {"Local Justificat